  "review": {
    "en": "A verse letter of advice to a family of would-be poets, easy in tone and full of craft: keep a work whole, suit style to subject, revise for years, mix the useful with the pleasing. It is less a theory than a working poet's table talk, and for centuries Europe's schools learned poetry from it.",
    "zh": "这是一封写给一家有志作诗者的诗体书信，口吻从容，满是手艺上的忠告：作品要统一完整，文体要合乎题材，要多年修改，要寓教于乐。它与其说是理论，不如说是一位行家的席间闲谈，欧洲的学校却凭它教了好几个世纪的诗。"
  },
